WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:05.969
Hey guys, it's Justine, and I thought it would be really fun to do a year and seven month review of the AirPods.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.599
I've had them since the very beginning and I think since the beginning,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.360
especially right when I first got them, I had some mixed reviews

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:19.980
because for whatever reason, they would not stay in my ears. But now I think my ears have officially conformed to the AirPods.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.140
And it's kind of crazy because I go running with them now, I work out.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.820
I do all kinds of activities and they stay in my ear.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:27.760
It's kind of shocking.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.460
Very surprising especially because of the struggle that I had when I first got them.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:38.640
So the AirPods and I definitely had a rocky first start off to our relationship because like I said, they didn't stay in my ears.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.500
But now they do so problem solved.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.200
They kept falling out in the most random and terrible places to fall out.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.360
The first one being on airplanes.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:53.000
I have crawled under so many seats. And especially in some of the seats when they get really wedged in there.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:57.239
It's almost impossible to get out. I've had to have flight attendants help me. I've had to have flashlights,

00:00:57.239 --> 00:01:00.479
I've had strangers digging on the ground, trying to help me find my AirPods.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.629
So the first time that I'd lost my entire set of AirPods,

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:09.329
I was traveling and I just got back from Hawaii and I looked in my purse and I realized my AirPods aren't here.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.799
I just got to the airport and I thought this is a problem because they're already sold out,

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:17.069
so even if I were to try to buy some now.
Even from the Apple store,

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:21.269
I wasn't gonna get them for another several months. That's how backorder they were originally.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:25.560
So I freaked out as any Apple fan would who became obsessed with their AirPods.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:30.629
I ordered a pair on eBay and they basically shipped the next day and I had them within three days.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.640
I made a video I was freaking out,

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:36.930
I was upset, of course, I was being overdramatic just as iJustine would. And then,

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:43.889
I'd say maybe a month later, I found them. That meant that I now have two pairs of AirPods.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:49.409
Which is actually quite helpful because I would always keep one of these inside of my laptop case.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.048
So no matter what I'd always have a set with me when I was away.

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:56.008
The other one stays in my purse. That leads me to maybe another month or two later,

00:01:56.008 --> 00:02:02.580
I thought that I had lost them again. I tweeted about it. I was upset, of course, overdramatic yet again.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.860
But it was okay because I had the backup one. It all was well. Having two is definitely not necessary,

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.980
but of course I'm not complaining because it has been nice. And you're probably saying: well, Justine you still have two.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.860
That's right because the missing AirPods

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:20.880
actually was found inside of my purse inside of like this secret little pocket that I didn't even know existed.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.880
So back at two AirPods.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.520
I tried a bunch of different AirPod accessories.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.540
I tried a little string that wraps around your head and I was like, this is stupid.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:33.720
Does this look good? They both fell out. I mean the good news is - oh gosh - if they fall out, they're both together.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.280
If I tie this like arou... That's not gonna work.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.300
My head's not... If it was a little bit bigger.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.560
I also had one AirPod stop working.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.040
Which was very upsetting because I was on a trip with my family actually, ironically going back to Hawaii.

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:49.768
If you guys haven't noticed, Hawaii is one of my favorite places in the entire world. I just love it.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:54.209
Every time I go there I'm just instantly happy and overjoyed and inspired. I need to move there.

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:55.820
But while we were on the plane over there,

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:00.320
I was so sad because one of my air pod stopped working. Just completely, entirely stopped.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.280
The good news, we were traveling to Oahu and there are two Apple Stores on that island.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.020
So as soon as we landed, I made a Genius Bar appointment.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:12.460
Went in, they replaced one of my AirPods and all was well. Trying to think if there's any other crazy AirPod stories.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:19.520
There has been times where I'll be eating something and I'll have my AirPods just sitting here. I'll take them out,

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:24.340
I'll be like eating some snacks or something. And I can't even tell you, this has happened more than once,

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.020
than I'd like to admit that I've almost

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:31.469
eaten an AirPod because I keep thinking it's like some sort of like a sweet treat like a little snack.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.079
Like I don't know what type of candy this would be. Like a popcorn.

00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:39.689
I've also thought that this was like dental floss before. I'd also thought it was a pack of gum or like some Tic Tacs.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.320
But no, AirPods.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:46.589
Something that I'm really looking forward to, which I feel like Apple hasn't really been talking about, is the Powermat or the AirPower.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:51.269
I call it something wrong every single time. So the next version of AirPods, it'll have wireless charging.

00:03:51.269 --> 00:03:56.669
So with the Powermat you'll be able to charge your AirPods, your watch and your phone, all at the same time.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:04.109
Which I'm just I'm honestly very excited for. I just hope that they announce something soon because I'm really really looking forward to it.

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:08.920
But yeah, just to be able to place these all down and have everything charge would be a dream come true.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.530
Hopefully we'll hear more about that soon. But in the meantime, I'm still loving my AirPods.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:19.140
Like I actually haven't found another pair of headphones that I like more. Don't know if I could even live without them.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.840
I mean, I'm sure I could but do I want to? No.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.660
The only time that I use real headphones is when I'm gaming. If I'm editing, I do need to use headphones

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:30.480
because sometimes the Bluetooth is lagging. And it doesn't have my edits on point with the music.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.160
So then I do have to use them.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.989
Even when I am editing, I end up just editing to the waveforms anyway, so it doesn't really make that much of a difference.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.700
I've been loving these things, I'm looking forward to the next version whenever that happens to be.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.920
Let me know in the comments below what you guys think. Do you love the AirPods? Do you not like them? Have you lost them?

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:51.080
How many have you lost. Surprisingly, I have bought these two and I have not officially,

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.600
permanently lost any of them. They've all made their way back to me.

